     9	## What the original claims, and what its numbers really are
    10	The indicator clusters swing highs/lows into price bands ("levels"), scores them, and signals a rejection candle at
    11	the nearest strong level. Its dashboard "win rate" is **the share of trades that touched TP1 (1R)**, not the share
    12	that made money: a trade that touches 1R and then stops at break-even counts as a win (it loses the fee). Intrabar it
    13	gives targets priority over stops (a bar that touches both counts the target), it enters at the signal close (market),
    14	and it has no fees, slippage or P&L. Its displayed stats cannot show profitability. Here every trade is a real 1-CL
    15	bracket with fees and the engine's worst-case intrabar order (stop first).
    16	
    17	## Hypothesis
    18	Prices where CL turned several times (and on bigger timeframes) hold orders: resting limit orders and stop clusters
    19	of earlier participants. When price comes back to such a level and the candle closes strongly away from it, the
    20	level held again; buying the retest/close with a stop beyond the wick should have positive expectancy.
    21	Who is on the other side: breakout traders who sold into support (bought into resistance) and get trapped.
    22	
    23	## Rules (long; short is the mirror)
    24	| Original (Pine) | CL version | Note |
    25	|---|---|---|
    26	| Swings: `ta.pivothigh/low(6, 6)` on the chart TF | owner-rule swing points on several TFs (`sources`): `all` = S..1d of {5m, 15m, 1h, 4h, 1d}, `htf` = only TFs above S | owner rule mandatory; no swing length |
    27	| Touch weight = 1 + reaction size (≤ 2.5 ATR) in the 6 confirmation bars | **weight = TF** (owner: the bigger the TF, the stronger the swing): 5m 1, 15m 1.5, 1h 2, 4h 3, 1d 3.5 (same 1..3.5 range as the original). Control `flat`: every TF weight 1 | ladder numbers are an assumption; only the order is the owner's |
    28	| A pivot counts once | one turning point counts once: same kind, same price, one candle nested in the other = same extreme; a higher TF confirming it later upgrades the weight (strength + Δw from then on, no backdating), no extra touch | Codex: keep `touches` an event count |
    29	| Swing known 6 bars after the extreme | `reg = lock`: touch when the point is locked (a newer opposite point exists above it, so rule 5 can no longer replace it). `reg = confirm`: touch when the point first appears (candle k+1 close); when it later leaves the structure (rule 5/4, while still in the top four points) its weight is withdrawn from the level from then on | lock is later but stable; confirm is earlier. Rule-4 removal of an already locked point is not withdrawn in lock mode (43 of 14,561 5m points in 2010) |
    30	| Level engine per chart bar | per completed candle of the signal TF `sig_tf` S ∈ {5m, 15m, 1h}: age (half-life 500 S bars) and cross (close beyond the band: ×0.7 strength) with the candle close, register touches known by its completion, merge overlapping bands (5 passes), cap 60 levels, drop strength < 0.25, pick the 3 nearest active (≥ 2 touches) levels per side | constants as original |
    31	| Band: weighted mean ± weighted std, clamped to [0.15, tol] × ATR34; join radius tol × ATR34 | same, ATR34 of S | `tol` ∈ {0.4, 0.6, 1.0} |
    32	| Score = 100·(1 − e^(−strength·polar/6)), polar ×1.25 if touched by highs and lows | same | `score` ∈ {0, 50, 70} minimum |
    33	| Buy rejection: price above the band before this bar, low into the band, close above the band, (close − low)/range ≥ clv, cooldown 10 bars per level, nearest level first, long wins a tie | same | `clv` ∈ {0.6, 0.75} |
    34	| Entry at the signal close (market) | limit only (`entry`): `close` = limit at the signal candle close; `band` = limit at the band top (retest). Works one S interval (clock minutes) from the next 1m bar; killed by a target touch; engine cancels at day change / roll / 15:10 CT | owner rule: limit entries, touch fills |
    35	| SL wick-anchored: min(low − 0.25·ATR14, entry − 0.5·ATR14) | `stop`: `wick` = same (ATR14 of S, vs the limit price); `band` = min(band low − 0.25·ATR14, entry − 0.5·ATR14) | risk < 5 ticks skipped |
    36	| TP 1R/2R/3R, BE after TP1, close at TP3 or reversal | `exit`: `r1`, `r2`, `r3` fixed target; `be3` = 3R target, stop to entry once a bar after the fill bar reached 1R (effective next bar; the fill-bar high is ignored because it may predate the fill). Opposite-signal reversal not modelled (one position at a time) | 1 contract |
    37	| any time | `session`: `all` (any signal 17:00..15:10 CT) or `rth` (signal candle completes 08:30..13:30 CT). Levels always evolve on all hours | RTH known from earlier studies (post-hoc prior) |
    38	
    39	Point-in-time: a swing candle k's state is known when candle k+1 completes (`avail`); orders work from the next 1m
    40	bar. A signal candle that straddles a roll or completes in the next session is skipped.
    41	Rolls (prices not back-adjusted): levels, ATR and touches reset at every contract change; a touch needs its extreme
    42	candle and its left reference candle inside the current contract. Owner swing structure itself runs on unchanged.
